      "writtenOn": "2022-03-18T18:11:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "```\nif !device_added.lock().unwrap().insert(\u0026addr) {\n  return False; \n}\n```\n\nhttps://doc.rust-lang.org/std/collections/struct.HashSet.html#method.insert\n\nWhile `added` is in scope, you have the lock acquired until you drop `added`. To avoid a future deadlock (since you also acquire the `callbacks` lock), it\u0027s better to drop the scope right away.",
      "revId": "1c5d25c86dfd999cbff5591d795f591109d0d0f5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "96acfe2d_df8a4d9c",
